1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,647
Chapter-13. 
Ethan Bruce POV

2
00:00:02,647 --> 00:00:04,037
I tore the bedroom apart.

3
00:00:04,037 --> 00:00:05,976
I didn't know what I was searching for.

4
00:00:05,976 --> 00:00:07,972
Maybe a sign that she was coming back.

5
00:00:07,972 --> 00:00:09,214
Maybe a ticket stub.

6
00:00:09,214 --> 00:00:10,497
Maybe just a mistake.

7
00:00:10,497 --> 00:00:14,141
I ripped the drawers out of her dresser and overturned them onto the floor.

8
00:00:14,141 --> 00:00:14,753
Empty.

9
00:00:14,753 --> 00:00:16,585
No clothes.No jewelry.

10
00:00:16,585 --> 00:00:19,905
Even the silk scarves I had bought her in Milan were gone.

11
00:00:19,905 --> 00:00:22,007
She had taken everything that was hers.

12
00:00:22,007 --> 00:00:24,173
And she had left everything that was mine.

13
00:00:24,173 --> 00:00:25,889
I stalked to the nightstand.

14
00:00:25,889 --> 00:00:31,939
The ring sat there.A five-carat diamond that I had slid onto her finger with a promise to cherish her.

15
00:00:31,939 --> 00:00:35,585
Now, it looked like nothing more than a shard of glass.Cold.Dead.

16
00:00:35,585 --> 00:00:37,088
Next to it was the paper.

17
00:00:37,088 --> 00:00:38,376
I picked it up again.

18
00:00:38,376 --> 00:00:39,363
You chose.

19
00:00:39,363 --> 00:00:40,244
Two words.

20
00:00:40,244 --> 00:00:43,073
No anger.No accusations.Just a fact.

21
00:00:43,073 --> 00:00:44,970
I crumpled the paper in my fist.

22
00:00:44,970 --> 00:00:46,137
"I didn't choose her!"

23
00:00:46,137 --> 00:00:47,863
I roared at the silence.

24
00:00:47,863 --> 00:00:49,774
"I chose duty!I chose honor!"

25
00:00:49,774 --> 00:00:52,823
My voice echoed against the bare walls, mocking me.

26
00:00:52,823 --> 00:00:54,519
But the truth festered in my gut.

27
00:00:54,519 --> 00:00:56,987
Duty to a woman who had manipulated me.

28
00:00:56,987 --> 00:01:00,152
Honor to a ghost of a man who died ten years ago.

29
00:01:00,152 --> 00:01:05,272
And in exchange, I had sacrificed the woman who washed the blood off my hands every night.

30
00:01:05,272 --> 00:01:06,470
I grabbed my phone.

31
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:09,402
"Capo," I snarled the second the line connected.

32
00:01:09,402 --> 00:01:09,976
"Boss?"

33
00:01:09,976 --> 00:01:11,382
"Wake them up.Everyone.

34
00:01:11,382 --> 00:01:13,434
I want every soldier on the pavement.

35
00:01:13,434 --> 00:01:17,288
I want eyes on every train station, airport, and bus terminal.

36
00:01:17,288 --> 00:01:19,446
Nothing moves without us knowing."

37
00:01:19,446 --> 00:01:21,851
"Sir, it's 2 AM.What's the target?"

38
00:01:21,851 --> 00:01:22,595
"My wife."

39
00:01:22,595 --> 00:01:25,508
There was a pause.Heavy.Hesitant."Mrs. Bruce?"

40
00:01:25,508 --> 00:01:29,635
"Find her.If anyone touches a hair on her head, I will skin them alive.

41
00:01:29,635 --> 00:01:31,384
And find the gray sedan.

42
00:01:31,384 --> 00:01:32,905
License plate unknown.

43
00:01:32,905 --> 00:01:35,487
It picked her up on the I-95 on-ramp."

44
00:01:35,487 --> 00:01:35,957
"On it."

45
00:01:35,957 --> 00:01:36,593
I hung up.

46
00:01:36,593 --> 00:01:39,321
The next forty-eight hours were a blur of hell.

47
00:01:39,321 --> 00:01:41,038
I didn't sleep.I didn't eat.

48
00:01:41,038 --> 00:01:46,702
I sat in the command center, my eyes burning as I watched the city through a thousand camera lenses.

49
00:01:46,702 --> 00:01:48,283
My men tore New York apart.

50
00:01:48,283 --> 00:01:49,533
They kicked down doors.

51
00:01:49,533 --> 00:01:50,955
They shook down snitches.

52
00:01:50,955 --> 00:01:52,689
They bribed harbor masters.

53
00:01:52,689 --> 00:01:53,355
Nothing.

54
00:01:53,355 --> 00:01:54,479
She was a ghost.

55
00:01:54,479 --> 00:01:58,695
The gray sedan had vanished into a blind spot near the tunnel.No plates.

56
00:01:58,695 --> 00:02:00,290
No facial recognition.

57
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:02,669
Whoever picked her up knew what they were doing.

58
00:02:02,669 --> 00:02:04,190
They knew our blind spots.

59
00:02:04,190 --> 00:02:05,581
"Casper," I whispered.

60
00:02:05,581 --> 00:02:08,613
The name floated up from the back of my mind, unbidden.

61
00:02:08,613 --> 00:02:10,606
The art curator.The civilian.

62
00:02:10,606 --> 00:02:13,441
The man she smiled at when she thought I wasn't looking.

63
00:02:13,441 --> 00:02:15,269
I ordered a team to his apartment.

64
00:02:15,269 --> 00:02:16,836
They found it scrubbed clean.

65
00:02:16,836 --> 00:02:19,913
He had left for a "sabbatical" in Europe two days ago.

66
00:02:19,913 --> 00:02:20,849
It was planned.

67
00:02:20,849 --> 00:02:26,345
While I was buying Ilene jewelry to keep her calm, Aurora was planning her escape with another man.

68
00:02:26,345 --> 00:02:30,648
I felt a surge of jealousy so potent it tasted like copper on my tongue.

69
00:02:30,648 --> 00:02:33,121
But beneath the jealousy, there was something else.

70
00:02:33,121 --> 00:02:33,795
Hunger.

71
00:02:33,795 --> 00:02:35,900
My stomach cramped, but not for food.

72
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:39,021
I looked at the surveillance photo of Aurora from the Gala.

73
00:02:39,021 --> 00:02:41,788
The one taken right before I threw the picture at her.

74
00:02:41,788 --> 00:02:43,475
She looked thin.Pale.

75
00:02:43,475 --> 00:02:45,202
Her eyes were dark hollows.

76
00:02:45,202 --> 00:02:50,555
I had been so busy managing Ilene's fake crises that I hadn't noticed my wife fading away.

77
00:02:50,555 --> 00:02:51,669
I had starved her.

78
00:02:51,669 --> 00:02:54,622
Not of food, but of me.Of safety.Of respect.

79
00:02:54,622 --> 00:02:58,431
I sat back in the leather chair, the material groaning under my weight.

80
00:02:58,431 --> 00:03:00,958
"You chose," I whispered to the glowing screen.

81
00:03:00,958 --> 00:03:02,103
I closed my eyes.

82
00:03:02,103 --> 00:03:03,184
I chose wrong.
